.TH QFW-DASHBOARD-ENABLE 8 "September 2026" "QFw 0.1" "Administration"
.SH NAME
qfw-dashboard-enable \- install the optional cluster dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-dashboard-enable
.RI [ --dry-run ]
.RI [ --host " address" ]
.RI [ --port " port" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initializes the pinned ElectroBoy submodule when needed and installs only
ElectroBoy core, reusable modules, and the qfw-slurm-cluster workflow in a
dashboard-local virtual environment. Normal cluster build and startup are not
invoked.
.SH SECURITY
The listener is restricted to loopback. Remote access requires a separately
configured authenticated reverse proxy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-dashboard-service (8),
.BR qfw-dashboard-disable (8)
